{"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When vector collections expand beyond tens of thousands of items, exact (O(N)) linear scans become a major latency bottleneck for real-time recommendation and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) systems.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"HNSWIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" actor provides a hierarchical graph-based spatial partitioning index with sub-millisecond query latency and logarithmic (O(\\log N)) search scaling.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Hierarchical-Navigable-Small-World-Architecture","text":"Hierarchical Navigable Small World Architecture"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"HNSW constructs a hierarchy of graph layers:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Top Layers (Sparse)","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Contain widely spaced long-range highway edges for rapid coarse geometric routing across distant clusters."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Intermediate Layers","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Progressively decrease edge length while increasing vertex density."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Bottom Layer (Layer 0, Dense)","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Contains all indexed vertices connected by dense short-range edges for high-accuracy localized nearest-neighbor refinement."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["Layer 2 (Express):   [A] ───────────────────────────► [F]","                      │                                │","                      ▼                                ▼","Layer 1 (Regional):  [A] ──────────► [C] ────────────► [F]","                      │               │                │","                      ▼               ▼                ▼","Layer 0 (Base):      [A] ──► [B] ──► [C] ──► [D] ──► [E] ──► [F]"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Key-Configuration-Parameters","text":"Key Configuration Parameters"},{"alignments":["left","left","left"],"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Recommended Default"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Impact on Search Quality & Index Build Time"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"M"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"16"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maximum outgoing connections per node. Higher values improve recall at the cost of higher memory and index construction time."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"efConstruction"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"200"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Size of dynamic candidate evaluation queue during insertion. Larger values produce higher-quality graph connectivity."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"efSearch"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"50"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dynamic queue size during search traversal. Higher values increase search recall towards 100% exact match."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"metric"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".euclideanDistance"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choice of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".euclideanDistance"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cosineSimilarity"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dotProduct"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]]]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Example-Usage","text":"Example Usage"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftCluster","","\/\/ 1. Initialize the actor-isolated index","let hnsw = HNSWIndex(metric: .cosineSimilarity, M: 16, efConstruction: 200, efSearch: 50)","","\/\/ 2. Add embeddings asynchronously","await hnsw.add(id: \"doc_news_1\", vector: [0.12, 0.94, -0.31], metadata: [\"category\": \"news\"])","await hnsw.add(id: \"doc_tech_2\", vector: [-0.85, 0.11, 0.52], metadata: [\"category\": \"technology\"])","","\/\/ 3. Query Top-K nearest neighbors","let queryEmbedding = [0.10, 0.90, -0.30]","let matches = await hnsw.search(query: queryEmbedding, topK: 5)","","for match in matches {","    print(\"Matched: \\(match.id) with score: \\(match.score)\")","}"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Thread-Safety--Swift-6-Strict-Concurrency","text":"Thread Safety & Swift 6 Strict Concurrency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"HNSWIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is implemented as an isolated Swift ","type":"text"},{"code":"actor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", guaranteeing thread safety and eliminating race conditions when multiple background tasks insert items or execute queries concurrently.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/hnswvectorsearch"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Scale approximate nearest neighbor (ANN) retrieval logarithmically using Hierarchical Navigable Small World graphs.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Spatial-Indexing","title":"Spatial Indexing","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/HNSWIndex","doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/do